.TH ZERODDS-XRCE-AGENTD 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-xrce-agentd \- DDS-XRCE agent daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-xrce-agentd
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIudp|tcp\fR:\fIADDR\fR]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-check\-config\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-xrce-agentd
is the Agent side of OMG DDS-XRCE 1.0: it represents one or more
eProsima-compatible Micro Clients (UDP, TCP or serial) in the DDS data
space, running the CREATE_CLIENT/STATUS_AGENT handshake, reliable streams
with HEARTBEAT/ACKNACK, FRAGMENT reassembly, and mapping CREATE/DELETE/
WRITE_DATA/READ_DATA onto real DDS participants, topics, publishers,
subscribers, data writers and data readers. A participant joins the DDS
domain its CREATE carries.
Implements
.IR docs/specs/dds-xrce-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the config file (YAML). See
.BR zerodds-xrce-agentd.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIudp|tcp\fR:\fIADDR\fR
Add a listener (repeatable). Default, if none is given anywhere: one UDP
listener on
.IR 0.0.0.0:2018 ,
eProsima's own default agent port.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM stops the daemon.
SIGHUP reloads what can be reloaded without a restart:
.BR log_level ", "
.BR limits.* ", "
.BR session_timeout_secs " and "
.BR discovery.enabled
(the discovery responder thread is stopped or started to match). A changed
.BR listeners: ", "
.BR type_files: " or "
.B xml_profile_files:
entry is logged and ignored until restart — live-rebinding a listening
socket or swapping the TypeObject set under in-flight sessions would risk
silently orphaning them. A configuration that does not load changes
nothing; the daemon keeps running on the last good configuration and logs
why the reload was refused.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Bind error \(em a listener's port already in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery or runtime error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/xrce-agentd.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-xrce-agentd.yaml (5),
DDS-XRCE 1.0 (OMG formal/2023-03-01).
